## Evidence

<!--
Mandatory anti-hallucination gate. Algorithm implementations get ported to
production systems. Wrong complexity claims or buggy snippets = silent
production failure. Crypto section is especially critical — see warnings.
-->

- **Overall status**: `verified` | `estimated` | `mixed` *(pick one)*
- **Source repo**: `<path or URL>` — `<sha or tag>` [verified|estimated]
- **Complexity validation**: `<e.g. cProfile, hyperfine, analytical proof>` [verified|estimated]
- **Property tests**: `<e.g. hypothesis, property-based test suite>` [verified|estimated]

### Evidence rules

- Implementation blocks in `### 2.x` MUST be verbatim from cited `file:line` (no pseudo-code).
- Complexity claims MUST cite either an empirical benchmark OR analytical proof.
- "Tests / properties" MUST be backed by a real test (not invented properties).
- Crypto section (3) MUST include independent audit reference for any hash/signature/KDF.
- If 0% of references are tagged, the catalog is editorial — re-verify against source + benchmarks.

## Como usar este documento

- **Audience**: dev procurando algoritmo pronto (crypto, search, sort, parsing) para reusar.
- **Next action**: revisar `## 3. Crypto & hashing` antes de QUALQUER decisão de segurança; rodar testes de propriedade do `### 2.x` antes de portar.
- **Quando re-verificar**: quando houver CVE em primitive cripto, ou quando benchmark mostrar regressão.

